274	39	40	6000000001303212	[Uni - Jan till Jun 2027] Robotics and Physical AI Engineer Intern	Singapore, sg	\N	https://api.smartrecruiters.com/v1/companies/NCS3/postings/6000000001303212	active	\N	2026-09-24 16:35:52.305886+08	2026-09-24 16:35:52.305886+08	2026-09-29 01:14:57.823611+08	2026-10-13 22:25:58.396487+08	As a Robotics and Physical AI Engineer Intern, you will be involved in cutting-edge deep tech development of robotics and physical AI systems that mimic human movement and behavior. You'll contribute to building advanced humanoid robotic systems through hands-on work across the full project lifecycle—from planning and simulation to deployment and maintenance. This is an opportunity to work on real-world applications that bridge high-level AI reasoning with physical motor control, bringing intelligent robots to life. Intern's Job Scope You will work across various subsystems of robotics and physical AI, with responsibilities including: Simulation & Environment Development Design 3D training environments (homes, factories, stairs) using NVIDIA Isaac Sim, Gazebo, or Unity Build and validate robot behaviors in high-fidelity simulation environments before physical deployment Create simulation-ready meshes using CAD software (SolidWorks, Autodesk Fusion 360, Blender) Implement 3D sensor models (LiDAR, depth cameras, IMUs) with realistic noise profiles Generate synthetic data and apply domain randomization techniques Control & Locomotion Develop algorithms for stable bipedal walking, balancing, and recovery from disturbances Apply reinforcement learning (RL) and whole-body control strategies Refine forward and inverse kinematics for human-like movement with high degrees of freedom Author and maintain robot description files (URDF & SDFormat) defining kinematics, joint limits, and inertial properties AI Integration & Safety Bridge high-level AI (vision-language models) with physical motor control Implement robust safety and fallback systems to prevent physical damage or injury when AI models behave unpredictably Develop platform orchestration layers managing communication between AI reasoning and motor control with low latency Hardware-Software Integration Collaborate with mechanical and electrical teams to integrate sensors and actuators using ROS 2 Maintain digital twin synchronization between 3D simulation models and physical hardware Design and maintain APIs for subsystem integration Work with projective geometry, coordinate transforms (TF2 in ROS), and mesh format conversions (STL, OBJ, USD, Collada) Software Engineering & Testing Emphasize code maintainability, version control (Git), and CI/CD pipelines Design monitoring tools and fail-safe layers Work with containerization (Docker) for consistent software deployment Develop test frameworks for system validation\n\nCurrently pursuing a Bachelor's degree in: Robotics Artificial Intelligence Computer Science Product Development Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) Mechanical Engineering (ME) Related fields Able to commit to a minimum of 6 months full-time internship Technical Skills (At least 2 competencies required) AI/ML Frameworks: Experience with reinforcement learning and imitation learning Programming: Proficiency in Python (model training) and/or C++ (real-time system integration) Robotics Middleware: Knowledge of ROS/ROS 2 for integrating AI with sensors and actuators Computer Vision: Skills in 3D scene reconstruction, object detection, spatial reasoning, OpenCV, CUDA, and TensorRT Embedded Systems: Understanding of Linux-based edge computing, GPU acceleration (CUDA), and real-time data transport protocols Simulation Tools: Familiarity with physics engines (MuJoCo, PhysX), VR/metaverse platforms (Unity), or CAD software (SolidWorks) Operating Systems: Linux (Ubuntu) and/or real-time operating systems (RTOS) Containerization: Experience with Docker Mathematics: Understanding of projective geometry and coordinate transforms Hardware Acceleration: Experience with NVIDIA Jetson/Thor or similar edge devices\n\nWe are driven by our AEIOU beliefs—Adventure, Excellence, Integrity, Ownership, and Unity—and we seek individuals who embody these values in both their professional and personal lives. We are committed to our Impact: Valuing our clients, Growing our people, and Creating our future. Together, we make the extraordinary happen. Learn more about us at ncs.co and visit our LinkedIn career site. Scam Alert We are aware of fraudulent job offers and impersonations of NCS recruiters. Phishing emails using convincing-looking but fake addresses are also commonly used to trick you into thinking that they come from official NCS sources. Please note that all official communications from NCS Group will only be sent from verified corporate email addresses. Always check that the sender’s email address ends with the genuine NCS domain, @ncs.com.sg and beware of extra letters, symbols or misspellings. When in doubt, verify the sender’s identity by contacting us at reachus@ncs.com.sg.	ac59f060c241346ec67a2517f80f58478be0f1b1ff72a19e332c9e2742bf17b5	{"id": "6000000001303212", "name": "[Uni - Jan till Jun 2027] Robotics and Physical AI Engineer Intern", "uuid": "f344c3dd-18f5-496c-828d-9e2c9c2eaae4", "jobAd": {"sections": {"jobDescription": {"text": "<p>As a Robotics and Physical AI Engineer Intern, you will be involved in cutting-edge deep tech development of robotics and physical AI systems that mimic human movement and behavior. You'll contribute to building advanced humanoid robotic systems through hands-on work across the full project lifecycle—from planning and simulation to deployment and maintenance. This is an opportunity to work on real-world applications that bridge high-level AI reasoning with physical motor control, bringing intelligent robots to life.</p><p><strong>Intern's Job Scope</strong></p><p>You will work across various subsystems of robotics and physical AI, with responsibilities including:</p><p><u>Simulation &amp; Environment Development</u></p><ul><li>Design 3D training environments (homes, factories, stairs) using NVIDIA Isaac Sim, Gazebo, or Unity</li><li>Build and validate robot behaviors in high-fidelity simulation environments before physical deployment</li><li>Create simulation-ready meshes using CAD software (SolidWorks, Autodesk Fusion 360, Blender)</li><li>Implement 3D sensor models (LiDAR, depth cameras, IMUs) with realistic noise profiles</li><li>Generate synthetic data and apply domain randomization techniques</li></ul><p><u>Control &amp; Locomotion</u></p><ul><li>Develop algorithms for stable bipedal walking, balancing, and recovery from disturbances</li><li>Apply reinforcement learning (RL) and whole-body control strategies</li><li>Refine forward and inverse kinematics for human-like movement with high degrees of freedom</li><li>Author and maintain robot description files (URDF &amp; SDFormat) defining kinematics, joint limits, and inertial properties</li></ul><p><u>AI Integration &amp; Safety</u></p><ul><li>Bridge high-level AI (vision-language models) with physical motor control</li><li>Implement robust safety and fallback systems to prevent physical damage or injury when AI models behave unpredictably</li><li>Develop platform orchestration layers managing communication between AI reasoning and motor control with low latency</li></ul><p><u>Hardware-Software Integration</u></p><ul><li>Collaborate with mechanical and electrical teams to integrate sensors and actuators using ROS 2</li><li>Maintain digital twin synchronization between 3D simulation models and physical hardware</li><li>Design and maintain APIs for subsystem integration</li><li>Work with projective geometry, coordinate transforms (TF2 in ROS), and mesh format conversions (STL, OBJ, USD, Collada)</li></ul><p><u>Software Engineering &amp; Testing</u></p><ul><li>Emphasize code maintainability, version control (Git), and CI/CD pipelines</li><li>Design monitoring tools and fail-safe layers</li><li>Work with containerization (Docker) for consistent software deployment</li><li>Develop test frameworks for system validation</li></ul>", "title": "Job Description"}, "qualifications": {"text": "<ul><li>Currently pursuing a&#xa0;<strong>Bachelor's degree</strong>&#xa0;in:<ul><li>Robotics</li><li>Artificial Intelligence</li><li>Computer Science</li><li>Product Development</li><li>Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE)</li><li>Mechanical Engineering (ME)</li><li>Related fields</li></ul></li><li>Able to commit to a&#xa0;<strong>minimum of 6 months full-time</strong>&#xa0;internship</li></ul><p><u>Technical Skills (At least 2 competencies required)</u></p><ul><li><strong>AI/ML Frameworks:</strong>&#xa0;Experience with reinforcement learning and imitation learning</li><li><strong>Programming:</strong>&#xa0;Proficiency in Python (model training) and/or C++ (real-time system integration)</li><li><strong>Robotics Middleware:</strong>&#xa0;Knowledge of ROS/ROS 2 for integrating AI with sensors and actuators</li><li><strong>Computer Vision:</strong>&#xa0;Skills in 3D scene reconstruction, object detection, spatial reasoning, OpenCV, CUDA, and TensorRT</li><li><strong>Embedded Systems:</strong>&#xa0;Understanding of Linux-based edge computing, GPU acceleration (CUDA), and real-time data transport protocols</li><li><strong>Simulation Tools:</strong>&#xa0;Familiarity with physics engines (MuJoCo, PhysX), VR/metaverse platforms (Unity), or CAD software (SolidWorks)</li><li><strong>Operating Systems:</strong>&#xa0;Linux (Ubuntu) and/or real-time operating systems (RTOS)</li><li><strong>Containerization:</strong>&#xa0;Experience with Docker</li><li><strong>Mathematics:</strong>&#xa0;Understanding of projective geometry and coordinate transforms</li><li><strong>Hardware Acceleration:</strong>&#xa0;Experience with NVIDIA Jetson/Thor or similar edge devices</li></ul>", "title": "Qualifications"}, "companyDescription": {"text": "<p>NCS is a leading AI Tech Services company. With a 15,000-strong team across the Asia Pacific, NCS scales its platforms and capabilities to provide clients with greater agility and AI expertise across a range of Industries. Embracing a strong ecosystem of global partners, NCS transforms technology services delivery combining AI with digital resilience to drive real business impact. NCS is a subsidiary of the Singtel Group.</p>", "title": "Company Description"}, "additionalInformation": {"text": "<div sr-tagline=\\"\\"></div><p>We are driven by our AEIOU beliefs—Adventure, Excellence, Integrity, Ownership, and Unity—and we seek individuals who embody these values in both their professional and personal lives. We are committed to our Impact: Valuing our clients, Growing our people, and Creating our future.</p><p>&#xa0;</p><p>Together, we make the extraordinary happen.</p><p>&#xa0;</p><p>Learn more about us at ncs.co and visit our LinkedIn career site.</p><p>&#xa0;</p><p></p><p><u>Scam Alert</u></p><p>&#xa0;</p><p>We are aware of fraudulent job offers and impersonations of NCS recruiters. Phishing emails using convincing-looking but fake addresses are also commonly used to trick you into thinking that they come from official NCS sources.</p><p>&#xa0;</p><p>Please note that all official communications from NCS Group will only be sent from verified corporate email addresses. Always check that the sender’s email address ends with the genuine NCS domain, @ncs.com.sg and beware of extra letters, symbols or misspellings. When in doubt, verify the sender’s identity by contacting us at reachus@ncs.com.sg.</p><p></p><p></p>", "title": "Additional Information"}}}, "jobId": "e9388e00-150b-4105-9cf6-b9d69af9a609", "active": true, "company": {"name": "NCS", "identifier": "NCS3"}, "creator": {"name": "", "avatarUrl": ""}, "jobAdId": "bc46c7b0-2e99-4736-b52b-94f7cb09c66d", "applyUrl": "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/NCS3/6000000001436844--uni-jan-till-jun-2027-robotics-and-physical-ai-engineer-intern?oga=true", "function": {"id": "information_technology", "label": "Information Technology"}, "industry": {"id": "it_and_services", "label": "Information Technology And Services"}, "language": {"code": "en", "label": "English", "labelNative": "English (US)"}, "location": {"city": "Singapore", "hybrid": false, "remote": false, "country": "sg", "latitude": "1.2811866", "longitude": "103.8503404", "fullLocation": "Singapore, , Singapore"}, "refNumber": "REF1782G", "department": {"id": 6000000000102340, "label": "Others"}, "postingUrl": "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/NCS3/6000000001436844--uni-jan-till-jun-2027-robotics-and-physical-ai-engineer-intern", "visibility": "PUBLIC", "customField": [{"fieldId": "691b1a593b3befd0769aace8", "valueId": "a32d3d0f-e368-4f2a-a921-805295b10110", "fieldLabel": "Service Org", "valueLabel": "AIC"}, {"fieldId": "COUNTRY", "valueId": "sg", "fieldLabel": "Country/Region", "valueLabel": "Singapore"}, {"fieldId": "68b6fdb339264fc0afa900c8", "valueId": "default", "fieldLabel": "Brands", "valueLabel": "NCS"}, {"fieldId": "691b14303b3befd0769aace4", "valueId": "da96cac5-4ee2-48d0-bdcb-b636cc689f6e", "fieldLabel": "Employment Group", "valueLabel": "Intern"}, {"fieldId": "68b6fdb339264fc0afa900c9", "valueId": "6000000000102340", "fieldLabel": "Department", "valueLabel": "Others"}, {"fieldId": "691b1a2a2e1a5b69c566719c", "valueId": "3261017", "fieldLabel": "Centre Name", "valueLabel": "AI Factory (3261017)"}, {"fieldId": "691b19513b3befd0769aace7", "fieldLabel": "Cost Centre", "valueLabel": "200010102303"}], "referralUrl": "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/external-referrals/company/NCS3/publication/f344c3dd-18f5-496c-828d-9e2c9c2eaae4?dcr_ci=NCS3", "defaultJobAd": true, "releasedDate": "2026-09-25T03:38:59.028Z", "experienceLevel": {"id": "internship", "label": "Internship"}, "typeOfEmployment": {"id": "intern", "label": "Intern"}}	2026-09-24 16:35:52.305886+08
275	39	40	6000000001288481	[Uni - Jan till Jun 2027] AI Engineer Intern (Middleware)	Singapore, sg	\N	https://api.smartrecruiters.com/v1/companies/NCS3/postings/6000000001288481	active	\N	2026-09-24 16:35:52.305886+08	2026-09-24 16:35:52.305886+08	2026-09-29 01:14:57.823611+08	2026-10-13 22:25:58.479852+08	You will be part of the Middleware team supporting the technology roadmap across AI, Cloud, Event-Driven Architecture, API Management, Integration, Observability, and Automation. Working alongside experienced architects and engineers, you will help develop AI-powered tools, reusable technical assets, and solution accelerators that support real project delivery, solution design, and presales activities. Rather than building experimental AI prototypes, you will contribute to practical solutions that can be adopted across the organisation. Throughout the internship, you will gain hands-on experience with enterprise integration technologies, cloud platforms, AI, and modern software architecture while working in an Agile environment. What You'll Do Depending on project needs, you may be involved in: AI Solution Development Develop AI-powered assistants and agents to support solution design and engineering activities. Build and enhance Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) knowledge assistants using approved Middleware reference architectures. Prototype AI-enabled middleware solutions using technologies such as Model Context Protocol (MCP), AI Gateways, and Agentic AI. Solution Architecture & Integration Support the development of reusable architecture patterns, templates, and technical assets. Assist in designing API Gateway and enterprise integration solutions. Contribute to event-driven architecture designs using messaging platforms such as Kafka, Solace, RabbitMQ, Confluent, and IBM MQ. DevOps & Observability Support the creation of monitoring dashboards, observability patterns, and operational runbooks. Assist in documenting resiliency, security, and non-functional requirements (NFRs) for enterprise solutions. Research & Innovation Research emerging AI, cloud, integration, and automation technologies. Evaluate new tools and recommend improvements to Middleware capabilities. Contribute ideas that improve engineering productivity and solution delivery. Collaboration & Delivery Work with senior architects and engineers in Agile sprint teams. Participate in solution discussions, design reviews, sprint planning, and technical demonstrations. Develop reusable assets for internal adoption, project delivery, and presales demonstrations. Document technical designs, implementation guides, and best practices.\n\nBasic understanding of cloud platforms such as Azure or AWS. Knowledge of programming languages such as Python, Java, or JavaScript. Interest in Generative AI, Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and AI agents. Basic understanding of APIs, system integration, or automation technologies. Familiarity with DevOps concepts, CI/CD, monitoring, or observability is an advantage. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Curious and eager to explore emerging technologies. Good communication and teamwork skills. Willingness to learn enterprise integration platforms such as Kong, Solace, Kafka, Workato, and IBM MQ. Proactive, adaptable, and willing to take ownership of assigned work.\n\nWe are driven by our AEIOU beliefs—Adventure, Excellence, Integrity, Ownership, and Unity—and we seek individuals who embody these values in both their professional and personal lives. We are committed to our Impact: Valuing our clients, Growing our people, and Creating our future. Together, we make the extraordinary happen. Learn more about us at ncs.co and visit our LinkedIn career site. Scam Alert We are aware of fraudulent job offers and impersonations of NCS recruiters. Phishing emails using convincing-looking but fake addresses are also commonly used to trick you into thinking that they come from official NCS sources. Please note that all official communications from NCS Group will only be sent from verified corporate email addresses. Always check that the sender’s email address ends with the genuine NCS domain, @ncs.com.sg and beware of extra letters, symbols or misspellings. When in doubt, verify the sender’s identity by contacting us at reachus@ncs.com.sg.	d021e676bc3c524308a845c68ac34e4dc18163e8f8c01b079b7503b180f1f8c6	{"id": "6000000001288481", "name": "[Uni - Jan till Jun 2027] AI Engineer Intern (Middleware)", "uuid": "cefe174f-6420-4c6e-9060-aa2aa4b7a48d", "jobAd": {"sections": {"jobDescription": {"text": "<p>You will be part of the Middleware team supporting the technology roadmap across AI, Cloud, Event-Driven Architecture, API Management, Integration, Observability, and Automation.</p><p>&#xa0;</p><p>Working alongside experienced architects and engineers, you will help develop AI-powered tools, reusable technical assets, and solution accelerators that support real project delivery, solution design, and presales activities. Rather than building experimental AI prototypes, you will contribute to practical solutions that can be adopted across the organisation.</p><p>Throughout the internship, you will gain hands-on experience with enterprise integration technologies, cloud platforms, AI, and modern software architecture while working in an Agile environment.</p><p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><p>Depending on project needs, you may be involved in:</p><p>AI Solution Development</p><ul><li>Develop AI-powered assistants and agents to support solution design and engineering activities.</li><li>Build and enhance Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) knowledge assistants using approved Middleware reference architectures.</li><li>Prototype AI-enabled middleware solutions using technologies such as Model Context Protocol (MCP), AI Gateways, and Agentic AI.</li></ul><p>Solution Architecture &amp; Integration</p><ul><li>Support the development of reusable architecture patter